            <ArticleTitle>Blood loss at the time of dilation and evacuation at 16 to 22 weeks of gestation in women using low molecular weight heparin: a case series.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-56</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0010-7824(17)30433-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.contraception.2017.09.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Describe blood loss with surgical abortion ≥16weeks of gestation in anticoagulated patients.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="STUDY DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Clinicians involved in a professional listserv (2011-2013) reported cases of abortion ≥16weeks of gestation in anticoagulated women.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">All 7 patients were using or had recently discontinued low molecular weight heparin (LMWH). One patient was reported to have greater than anticipated blood loss for gestational age. No patients required transfusion and no complications were reported.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Our limited case series suggests D&amp;E may not always be contraindicated in women with recent or current LMWH use.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
